  "rule": "Select V41 only for resumed walking. For active, explicitly contact-bearing feet in stance phase 73..359, use all-four-leg floor-upright reference geometry at the actual measured torso height; retain V40 measured-pose goals for every unselected foot. Hold the current selector fixed for current and previous-wave goal evaluations. Keep all four constraints, original observations, upstream waves, reference slew, V40 absent-contact full-rate and other-contact wave-rate fallback, gains, caps, clocks, smooth lift and the original physical schedule/evaluator. Retain measured-pose baseline, upright reference, actual mixed goals and both plans under explicit receipt labels. This is a posture/contact-based reference, not a synthetic observation or real-time force-aware controller.",
  "parameter_basis": "No new gain, cap, timer, fitted correction or threshold. V41 changes only selected stance reference geometry using the already verified contract. Native probes on all 400 saved V40 inputs select 1037 stance-foot inputs; one-command substitution has 83 saturated commands, while chained references have 168 versus V40's 85, with 47 selector transitions and 102 unselected commands affected by prior changed references. These are old-state command probes, not a physical prediction.",
  "compatibility_scope": "Distinct V41 policy/profile/memory/receipt identities. Keep original floor-v2 requests, finite translation-only box-floor provenance, native contacts, unchanged upstream wave/gate memory and exact independent replay. Its new optional upright_stance receipt distinguishes measured baseline, upright reference and actual selected goals. Four thousand older-policy native outputs and six recovery fixtures remain exact; all old physical records, contracts and runtime images are immutable.",
